{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Plan-review PASSED (certified) — child-roster coverage gap flagged for post-approval execution planning\n\n`rebar review-plan polite-antivirus-bedbug` verdict = **PASS**, attestation **certified** (verified_at_sha `af915ac63`, currency_basis `file_impact`). Epic claimed → `in_progress`. **0 blocking**, **7 advisory** findings. The advisories do not block certification but MUST be resolved when execution slices are (re)scoped after human approval — capturing them here so they are durable:\n\n1. **The broadened rewrite mechanism is owned by NO existing child.** Children 866f (ADR), 51a7, e32d, aff9 are all scoped to `.retired` **tombstone** GC. None names the publish-swap CAS, S3 exclusive bundle-set replacement (auto-doctor bypass), core-git `fast-import` rewrite primitive, or ledger `position→commit_sha` re-resolution / `enforce_since` re-anchor. **This is the crux of the whole proof:** `.retired` GC shrinks the *blobless* guarded pack by ~0 (`.retired` files are blobs; the guarded pack has zero blobs), so the child union as currently scoped implements a lever the parent proof shows **cannot** meet the pack-shrink objective. The effective lever — commit/tree history collapse — has no owning child yet.\n2. **Pack-shrink quantification / budget items unowned:** the \"quantified vs 100 MiB\", \"coalescing insufficient at any safe horizon\", \"W3 budget-bridge\", and \"W1/W2 structural follow-ups\" ACs have no sibling owner (866f's ADR roster covers horizon/reachability/override/proof but not pack-size quantification).\n3. **C1–C5 at the rewrite level unproven by children:** 866f proves I1–I9 for the horizon+override and 51a7 on a reconvergence fixture, but no child proves C1–C5 specifically for the broadened commit/tree rewrite + SNAPSHOT authorship_ledger carriage, incl. the `<N-day clone with unpushed writes` case.\n4. **Rollback gap (post-reconcile clients):** rollback restores the backup ref / S3 rollback bundle prefix, but does not state a re-convergence path for clients that ALREADY reconciled onto the rewritten baseline (new SHAs) *before* a rollback — after rollback those clones point at a baseline graph the remote no longer has.\n5. **Human-approval gate not carried as a child precondition:** no implementation child (51a7/e32d/aff9) carries the HARD-STOP human-approval milestone as an explicit ordering dependency.\n\n**Disposition:** these are execution-planning corrections, to be applied when the epic's child roster is re-scoped AFTER human approval of this design. They reinforce the central escalation point — `.retired` GC alone is the wrong lever; the commit/tree-collapse rewrite is the real one, and it is the destructive action gated behind human approval. **HARD STOP holds: no S0–S3 implementation, no history rewrite, no force-push until approved.**"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788040400711589980,"uuid":"51761af1-8946-44e6-a1d3-50877d442235"}